        "id": "ch3_2-1",
        "text": "Selecting and sorting objects\nMany of the cmdlets we might run will produce a large amount of output, and, likely, much of it will\nnot be interesting. Therefore, it\u2019s useful to be able to select just the bits we need and sort them into\na meaningful order. There are two cmdlets for doing this: Select-Object and Sort-Object .\nWe will often see these referred to by their aliases \u2013 select and sort .\nThe PowerShell Pipeline \u2013 How to String Cmdlets Together\n56\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Using Select-Object\n\u2022 Ordering objects with Sort-Object\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
